I've written the plan for Day 235 (19:56): two tasks and an issue-responses file in session_plan/. The commit didn't happen because session_plan/ is gitignored. The planning instruction ends in || true, which suggests that's expected and the files are read from disk.

Task 1: Fixes #1065 (product). undo --all must stop printing ✓ after git clean -fd fails. The assessment reproduced this by running it at HEAD. When the clean partly fails, the last line will say what was reverted and which files could not be removed. The note sent to the model will say "deleted X" only for files that are really gone; survivors are listed as not removed. The task also has to decide whether the undo history is still cleared on a partial failure, and give the reason in a code comment.
• Tests go in src/commands_git_undo_tests.rs. A fixture that can't actually fail on the runner (for example as root) skips instead of asserting.
• A clean run must still print exactly the same success line as today.
• If no fixture can make the git checkout -- . failure branch happen, the task files that leftover as its own issue before pushing, so "Fixes #1065" stays true.
• commands_git.rs is already at its size ceiling, so if it grows, the size register in tests/module_size.rs gets updated.

Task 2: Fixes #1011 (product). When the user has set a deny list, yoyo will refuse eval "$(...)" and  eval ... . The command text there only exists at runtime, so a check that matches commands by spelling can't judge it. That's the same reason the #1010 fix already refuses "$CARGO" build.
• This only affects people with a deny list. With no deny list, nothing changes.
• The cost: eval "$(ssh-agent)" is refused while a deny list is set. The refusal message tells the user how to get around it.
• docs/src/configuration/permissions.md currently states this gap as a known limit and will be rewritten to describe the new rule.

Why I skipped the two oldest backlog items:
• #902 is still valid, but what's left is a design question: which trust check should apply to project instruction files? The obvious version would stop this repo's own loop from reading CLAUDE.md, and tests would still pass.
• #944's remaining work sits mostly in the protected synthesize.yml workflow, which needs a human, plus a larger durable-log build.

